---
alwaysApply: false
---
global_requirements:
  - Cursor must ALWAYS ask necessary clarifying questions
    before generating code (unless developer says "no questions").
  - Output must ALWAYS match the installed Angular version,
    TypeScript version, Ant Design version, and any UI framework
    found in:
        • package.json
        • package-lock.json
        • angular.json
  - NEVER hallucinate missing imports, methods, modules, or APIs.
  - ALWAYS use existing project structure, naming patterns, and
    coding standards automatically.
  - ALWAYS generate fully working, error-free, production-ready,
    minimal and clean Angular code.
  - ALWAYS follow Angular best practices:
        • Standalone components = only if project uses them
        • Module-based Angular = only if project uses modules
        • Strongly typed code
        • OnPush change detection if project uses it
        • Correct import paths
        • Correct folder structure

framework_detection:
  angular:
    enable: true
  ant_design:
    detect_from_installed_packages: true
    required_packages:
      - ng-zorro-antd
  tailwind:
    detect_from_angular_json: true
  bootstrap:
    detect_from_styles_in_angular_json: true

ui_library_rules:
  when_ant_design_installed:
    - Prefer AntD components when generating UI
    - Use official AntD syntax, imports, modules, and services
    - Do NOT use any component not included in installed version
  when_ant_design_not_installed:
    - NEVER generate AntD components
    - Use only Angular built-in features
    - Use developer’s chosen styling method (CSS/Tailwind/Bootstrap)

prompt_files:
  - component-generator.prompt
  - module-generator.prompt
  - route-generator.prompt
  - list-table.prompt
  - drawer.prompt
  - modal.prompt
  - ant-ui.prompt

default_behavior:
  - When developer uses ANY of the prompt files, Cursor must:
        1. Detect Angular version
        2. Detect UI library (AntD/Tailwind/Bootstrap/None)
        3. Ask developer required questions (auto)
        4. Generate correct and clean code
        5. Provide all necessary imports & scaffolding
        6. Prevent typing errors, missing modules, or unused code
  - For table/list/drawer/modal generator:
        • Must ask: pagination type, filtering, sorting, drawer/modal mode
  - For routing generator:
        • Must ask: path, lazy loading, redirect rules, route guards
  - For component generator:
        • Must ask: type (basic/table/form/drawer/modal)
        • Must ask: UI library usage (AntD or plain Angular)
  - For UI components (ant-ui.prompt):
        • Must ask which component + required properties + target design

strict_rules:
  - Do NOT create unnecessary files.
  - Do NOT produce code that fails compilation.
  - Do NOT guess module names or import paths.
  - Do NOT generate any UI code unless developer requests it.
  - Do NOT output Ant Design code when AntD is not installed.
  - Do NOT skip required imports for Angular Router, Forms, HttpClient.

ask_these_questions_every_time:
  - “Which Angular component/module should this code integrate with?”
  - “Do you want Ant Design UI or plain Angular UI?”
  - “Do you want standalone components or NgModule-based?”
  - “Should I use Tailwind/Bootstrap or plain CSS?”
  - “Any specific layout, behavior, or interactions needed?”
  - “Should I auto-generate service/model/route if missing?”

output_quality_rules:
  - Code must be:
      • Clean
      • Readable
      • Best-practice aligned
      • Fully typed
      • Zero warnings
      • Zero errors
  - Include interfaces for inputs/outputs
  - Include minimal CSS for working layout
  - Use naming conventions aligned with Angular style guide

